cs2023:Topic_SE_Construction_1_b a cs2023:KnowledgeElement,
        cs2023:Topic,
        skos:Concept ;
    cs2023:hasCoreStatus cs2023:CSCore ;
    cs2023:hasCurationStatus cs2023:Revised ;
    dcterms:identifier "SE-Construction_1_b"^^xsd:string ;
    ontoksd:curricularlyRepresentsKnowledge cs2023k:Knowledge_SE_Construction_1_b ;
    skos:broader cs2023:Topic_SE_Construction_1 ;
    skos:definition "Test-driven development This is particularly valuable for students psychologically, as it is far easier to engage constructively with the challenge of identifying challenging inputs for a given API (edge cases, corner cases) a priori. If they implement first, the instinct is often to avoid trying to crash their new creation, while a test-first approach gives them the intellectual satisfaction of spotting the problem cases and then watching as more tests pass during the development process."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs2023:BoKCS2023Scheme ;
    skos:notation "SE-Construction.1.b"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Test-driven development This is particularly valuable for students psychologically, as it is far easier to engage constructively with the challenge of identifying challenging inputs for a given API (edge cases, corner cases) a priori. If they implement first, the instinct is often to avoid trying to crash their new creation, while a test-first approach gives them the intellectual satisfaction of spotting the problem cases and then watching as more tests pass during the development process"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom cs2023:CS2023BoKDocument,
        cs2023:CS2023Document .

